                <pb facs="0147" n="131" sameAs="frus:frus1951v07p1/pg131"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">795.00/1–2551: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bonsal</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-01-25T20:00:00+01:00">January 25, 1951—8
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4367. FonOff today showed us telegram January 19 from French Consul General
                    Shanghai, relayed through Peiping, substance of which as follows:</p>
                <p>According to “Chinese liberal” close to local Communist leaders, Chinese
                    Communists have just completed plan for intervention in IC through “volunteers”
                    but have given up idea carrying out such plan at present because of financial
                    and economic difficulties created by Chinese Communists intervention in Korea.
                    According several Chinese sources, strong pressure has very recently been
                    brought to bear on Peiping regime by “liberal circles and moderate Communist
                    elements” to moderate Chinese Communist attitude re Korea. These sources state
                    this pressure having an effect which should be reflected in Chinese Communist
                    reply to UN proposals for settlement Korean problem. Considerable financial
                    burden on economy as result Chinese Communist intervention Korea has played
                    major part in strengthening this pressure.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bonsal</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
